  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cbc795acf92c1fb48bae236e4ba4d39f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q07_Bias_Forward
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PNJunctionLab.AssessmentQuestion
  questionId: q07_fwd_bias
  topic: 3
  topicTag: 4. Forward & Reverse Bias
  shortSummaryLabel: Forward Bias Mechanism
  promptText: Connecting + to the P terminal and - to N applies forward bias (V > 0). How do barrier height, depletion width W, and current respond?
  options:
  - Barrier rises to V0 + V, W widens, and current remains zero
  - Barrier drops to V0 - V, W widens, blocking majority diffusion
  - Barrier drops to V0 - V, W narrows, and majority carriers cross exponentially
  - Built-in field flips instantly once V > 0.05 V
  correctIndex: 2
  explanation: Forward bias opposes the built-in field, lowering the barrier to V0 - V and narrowing W so majority carriers surge exponentially once past the diode knee (limited by a series resistor).
  recommendedStation: Station 5
